  DUT      : swi_d (AT-x960-56YSQ) console u2 at 115200, S/N A2WQS700B, standalone,
             Active Master, software sin_x96056-20261019-27
  artefact : an interface description with a unique text string. A description is
             visible in `show running-config`, it is kept by `write`, it does not affect
             forwarding, and nothing else on the device would ever write that text.
  stimulus : the DUT writes a log message for every CLI command it is given. A command
             that carries a chosen string is therefore the trigger's stimulus, produced
             on demand and timed to the second. No cable and no port flap are needed.
  tools    : tools/qmark.py (read CLI help, sends no carriage return);
             tools/ckcon.py, tools/cfg.py, tools/ckyn.py (console driving);
             tools/awshell.py (a `start-shell` root shell on the DUT, used to create the
             two `.scp` files and read them back);
             tools/ckreload.py (reload); tools/health.py (health reads)

